<h2 style="margin:0 0 4px;">💵 Payment structure</h2>
<p class="muted" style="margin:0 0 16px;">What a project submission pays once it's approved and published. The more complete the submission, the more it pays.</p>

<div class="card tier">
  <div class="tier-amount">$10</div>
  <div>
    <strong>The basics</strong>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:4px 0 0;font-size:13px;">Before + after photos and all required descriptions filled in (address, details, bullet notes).</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="card tier">
  <div class="tier-amount">$15</div>
  <div>
    <strong>Basics + extra photos</strong>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:4px 0 0;font-size:13px;">Everything above, plus one or more extra gallery photos.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="card tier">
  <div class="tier-amount">$20</div>
  <div>
    <strong>Basics + extra photos + video</strong>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:4px 0 0;font-size:13px;">Everything above, plus a job video (uploaded through the Videos page or a YouTube/Vimeo link on the project).</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="card tier tier-top">
  <div class="tier-amount">$25</div>
  <div>
    <strong>The full package</strong>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:4px 0 0;font-size:13px;">Everything above, plus a customer review (pasted review text on the project).</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="card" style="background:#f5f8fa;">
  <p style="margin:0;font-size:13px;line-height:1.7;color:#475569;">
    <strong>How it works:</strong> when your project is approved and published it shows on your dashboard with a red <span class="pay-badge pay-badge-unpaid" style="font-size:11px;">Unpaid</span> tag. The office reviews how complete the submission is, sets the amount, and marks it <span class="pay-badge pay-badge-paid" style="font-size:11px;">✓ Paid</span> — the row turns green and shows the amount you're getting. Amounts follow the tiers above; the office may adjust for exceptional submissions.
  </p>
</div>

<a class="btn btn-outline btn-block" href="/" style="text-align:center;margin-top:14px;">Back to dashboard</a>

